","The dietary condition that leads to the conversion of glucose to fatty acids in the body is **carbohydrate excess**. This occurs when the body consumes more glucose than it needs for energy. Excess glucose is converted into fatty acids through a process called gluconeogenesis, which occurs in the liver and muscles. These fatty acids can then be stored as triglycerides in adipose tissue or used as energy stores in the body. This process is common in obese individuals and those who consume a diet with an excess of carbohydrates.
