2. Prepare the activated carbon: Prepare a known amount of activated carbon (e.g., 0.5 g) and dry it at 105°C for 10 minutes to remove any moisture.

3. Set up the experimental conditions: Set up a series of batch reactors with the water sample and activated carbon. Adjust the pH (e.g., 3, 7, and 9) and temperature (e.g., 25, 40, and 60°C) for each reactor. Keep the initial dye concentration and activated carbon dosage constant.

