E°_cell = (+0.34 V) - (+0.0 V)
E°_cell = +0.34 V

Next, we need to determine the reaction quotient (Q). The balanced redox reaction is:

2H⁺ + Cu → Cu²⁺ + H₂

The reaction quotient (Q) is given by:

Q = [Cu²⁺]/[H₂]

Given the concentration of Cu²⁺ is 0.1 M and the hydrogen gas pressure is 1 bar (which can be converted to moles/L using the ideal gas law), we can calculate Q.

