An example of absolute asymmetric synthesis is the synthesis of the chiral auxiliary 1-phenylpyrrolidnylamine, which was achieved by the Meerwein-Ponndorf-Veriegler (MPV) reaction using a chiral catalyst. The reaction produced the desired enantiomer with 100% ee, demonstrating the ability of asymmetric synthesis to produce enantiomerically pure compounds.

