- **σ molecular orbitals** have electron density concentrated along the axis connecting the nuclei of the bonded atoms. This is a head-on overlap of atomic orbitals, resulting in a symmetrical electron density distribution.  
- **π molecular orbitals** have electron density concentrated above and below the axis connecting the nuclei of the bonded atoms. This is a side-by-side overlap of atomic orbitals, resulting in a non-symmetrical electron density distribution.  

