$$1.2 \times 10^{20} = \frac{x}{(1.0)(0.25)^6} \approx \frac{x}{1.5625 \times 10^{-4}}$$

Solving for x:

$$x \approx 1.2 \times 10^{20} \times 1.5625 \times 10^{-4} = 1.855 \times 10^{16} \text{ M}$$

Therefore, the change in equilibrium concentration of FeCN$_6^{4-}$ is approximately $\boxed{1.855 \times 10^{16} \text{ M}}$.
