c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
a) **Retrospective**  
   - The study examines prior beliefs and actions (smoking) to understand a current condition (bladder cancer).  

b) **Cross-sectional**  
   - The study measures both eating habits and general health at the same time (at a single point in time).  

c) **Prospective**  
   - The study observes a group over time to predict future symptoms (cancer) based on their eating and exercise patterns.  

d) **Comparative Comparison** (not listed as a category, but the most accurate).  
   - The study compares two existing sets of data (prices of general and named-brand items) at a known time.  

The answer d is not a standard type of time-based classification (e.g., cross-sectional, retrospective, prospective). However, it is a comparison of existing data, not a study of time-dependent changes.  

$\boxed{\text{a: Retrospective, b: Cross-sectional, c: Prospective, d: Comparison}}$

