**Explanation**:
1. **Definitions**:
   - \(L_{\alpha}\) is the \(\alpha\)-th layer of the L-series, which is a growing sequence of layers with \(L_0 = L_1 = 0\), and \(L_{\alpha} = \{X, \text{ where } X \text{ is a subset of } L_{\alpha-1}\text{ and } X \text{ is a member of } L_{\alpha-1}\text{, for all } \alpha > 0\).
   - \(V_{\alpha}\) is the \(\alpha\)-th Vaughan-type number, which is the number of elements in the \(\alpha\)-th star of the Vaughan-type series.
   - \(\phi_{\alpha}\) is the \(\alpha\)-th Binet number, which is the number of elements in the \(\alpha\)-th step of the Binet-sequence.

2. **Equality Condition**:
   - The equality \(\left|L_{\alpha}\right| = \left|V_{\alpha}\right\}\) holds if and only if the \(\alpha\)-th line of the L-series and the \(\alpha\)-th Vaughan-type number are identical.

