   - The equality \(\left|L_{\alpha}\right| = \left|V_{\alpha}\right\}\) holds if and only if \(\alpha = \phi_{\alpha}\) for all ordinives \(\alpha > \omega\). This is because the Binet numbers are equal to the Vaughan-type numbers and the L-series, and the Binet numbers are equal to \(\alpha\) only when \(\alpha\) is a Binet number.

Thus, the statement is correct. 

