","We start by finding $g(1458)$. Let $n = 3^k$ be the smallest positive integer such that $n > 1458$. Then, we have:
\[
g(1458) = g(3^{k-1} \cdot 3) = 4g(3^{k-1}) = 4^2g(3^{k-2}) = \cdots = 4^{k-1}g(3) = 4^{k-1}g(3).
\]
Since $g(3) = 2 - 2|3 - 2| = 0$, we have $g(1458) = 0$.

