\[
2 - 2|x - 2| = 0 \implies |x - 2| = 1 \implies x - 2 = \pm 1.
\]
Thus, $x = 3$ or $x = 1$. Since $x \geq 1$, the smallest such $x$ is $\boxed{1}$.
