\[
\liminf_{y \to x^*, y \in \mathcal{U}} \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\|y - x^*\|} \geq 0.
\]
Prove that if $f$ is Fréchet differentiable at $x^*$, then $f$ has the quasimin property at $x^*$ if and only if $\forall y \in \mathcal{U} : \nabla f(x^*)(y - x^*) \geq 0$.
