<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Calculate the energy released by the HMTD explosion:**
   - The energy released is given by \( E = \frac{P_2 V_2 - P_1 V_1}{1 - \gamma} \), where \( P_1 = 1.0 \text{ bar} \), \( P_2 = 1.0 \text{ kbar} = 1000 \text{ bar} \), \( V_1 = 1.0 \text{ L} \), and \( \gamma = 1.4 \).
   - Substituting the values:
     \[
     E = \frac{(1000 \text{ bar})(1.0 \text{ L}) - (1.0 \text{ bar})(1.0 \text{ L})}{1 - 1.4} = \frac{999 \text{ bar L}}{-0.4} = -2497.5 \text{ bar L}
     \]
