   \[
   0.56 = 1 - \frac{1}{R^{1.4 - 1}}
   \]
   Solving for \(R\):
   \[
   R = \left( \frac{1}{1 - 0.56} \right)^{1/0.4} = 3.56
   \]

2. **Work Done (W)**:
   The work done per kg of air is given by:
   \[
   W = \left(1 - \frac{1}{R^{\gamma - 1}}\right) \left(544 \text{ kJ/kg}\right)
   \]
   Substituting \(R = 3.56\):
   \[
   W = (1 - 1/3.56^{0.4}) \times 544 = 250.5 \text{ kJ/kg}
   \]

