\[
W = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v
\]
The rate of work done is:
\[
\frac{dW}{dt} = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v
\]
Since the work done is converted into heat, the rate of heat transfer is:
\[
Q = \frac{dW}{dt} = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{Q}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}
\]
The entropy production rate is \(\boxed{\dfrac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}}\).
